    "candidate": {
      "id": "recovery-after-single-drop",
      "property_ref": "client-operation-continuity",
      "inspiration_ref": "epoch-transition-state-reuse",
      "summary": "Suspected mechanism: after the coordinator's outbound message is dropped, a timer-driven leader handoff occurs before a majority has the operation; the new leader reuses accepted-suffix state from the older epoch, so the post-handoff decision may not be the same client operation.",
      "suspected_mechanism": "op-append [workload-invoked]: A single client operation is submitted to the current coordinator and becomes the command whose continuity is at risk. -\u003e lost-quorum-copy [message-dropped]: Dropping the coordinator's inflight message prevents the operation from reaching every participant before the timer-driven transition. -\u003e follower-timer [temporal-fired]: A follower's periodic pulse starts an election while the operation may be absent from its accepted suffix. -\u003e leader-handoff [coordinator-changed]: The leadership handoff occurs before a stable majority has the operation, so the new leader's reconciliation is the continuity point. -\u003e post-handoff-decide [decision-advanced]: A decision is taken after the handoff; if it advances a log position without the appended command, the client operation continuity hypothesis is exposed.",
      "mechanism_steps": [
        {
          "milestone_id": "op-append",
          "kind": "workload-invoked",
          "rationale": "A single client operation is submitted to the current coordinator and becomes the command whose continuity is at risk.",
